{"step_index":76,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-20T07:33:05Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-20T10:33:05+03:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-20T10:33:08+03:00\nCreated At: 2026-11-20T10:33:05+03:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-20T10:33:08+03:00\nThe search for \"\"killactive\" \"hyprlang2lua\" OR \"hyprland.lua\"\" returned the following summary:\nThe terms relate to the major transition in **Hyprland (v0.55+)** moving away from the legacy `hyprlang` format (`hyprland.conf`) to native **Lua configurations** (`hyprland.lua`)[1][2]. \n\nHere is how `killactive` maps and translates under this shift:\n\n### 1. The Migration Context (`hyprlang2lua`)\n[`hyprlang2lua`](https://github.com/EIonTusk/hyprlang2lua) is a utility tool designed to help users convert their old `hyprland.conf` files into the new Hyprland Lua format[1][3]. \n\n### 2. Translating `killactive` to Lua\nIn legacy configurations, closing the active window via dispatcher looked like this:\n```ini\nbind = $mainMod, Q, killactive,\n```\n\nIn the modern Hyprland Lua API format, legacy action names and dispatchers have been modernized or structured into helper functions (such as `hl.dsp.window.close()` or mapped dispatcher parameters)[1][4]:\n* **Legacy name:** `killactive` (which gracefully closes a window despite its name)[1]\n* **New Lua equivalent:** Maps to window closing routines like `.close()`[1] or `hl.dsp.window.close()` depending on how your keybind helper is structured[4]. \n\nIf you are using `hyprlang2lua` to automate the porting of your dotfiles, it automatically translates legacy vocabularies (like changing `killactive` over to the updated string/dispatcher format required by Hyprland 0.55+)[1].\n\nSources:\n[1] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHzBLF_kpxKMZ8wtlJ8sl6gGa3Q1wqyBzaw0Y9itGr7z4NLwWsU-5J5ZlmmTgkvqypCM0NwkKrFl_yjvnE0O0TAlsVXViXRiLvdcxxT8l4zEmRTZTD10F1CcKi-v7QY)\n[2] [hypr.land](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.goo